# MinIO data volume

This directory is the **MinIO storage volume** mounted into the
`eurio-minio` Docker container as `/data`.

⚠️ **DO NOT DELETE** ⚠️

What's in here:

```
data/
├── numista-canonical/   ← public Numista referential (jpg, ~1 GB)
├── enrichment-raws/     ← raw scraped photos (eBay, etc.)
└── enrichment-crops/    ← normalised 224×224 crops fed to training
```

This data is the **source of truth for the dev chain** (vision §"Cible
end-state"). The only safety net is the weekly tarball pushed to
pCloud by the systemd timer (see `infra/backup/`). There is no
versioning at the bucket level.

If you accidentally `git clean -fdx` or `rm -rf` this directory, you
lose up to 1 week of new uploads. The `.gitignore` keeps the actual
contents out of git but versioning **this file** ensures the
directory exists at clone time and gives you this warning.

Restore procedure: see `infra/minio/README.md` §"Restore from pCloud".
